    <textAnnotation id="An_Input">
      <text>Example input:
{
  "run": "stage"
}</text>
    </textAnnotation>
    <association id="As_An_Input" sourceRef="An_Input" targetRef="Ev_Start" />
    <textAnnotation id="An_T_Platform">
      <text>The version comes from the process that runs the test, not
from a page about the stand: the host's file version, as
on the API's Swagger page, and the engine's assembly
version.</text>
    </textAnnotation>
    <association id="As_An_T_Platform" sourceRef="An_T_Platform" targetRef="T_Platform" />
    <textAnnotation id="An_T_In_FirstFlow">
      <text>Every example is called as it is in this repository, with
its own example input, through a Call Activity to the Flow
of the same name in the tenant library.</text>
    </textAnnotation>
    <association id="As_An_T_In_FirstFlow" sourceRef="An_T_In_FirstFlow" targetRef="T_In_FirstFlow" />
    <textAnnotation id="An_T_Check_FirstFlow">
      <text>A check reads the answer: the failure branch's
ErrorResponse, no answer or an answer without the expected
marker is a failed check. Each line of the report says
which.</text>
    </textAnnotation>
    <association id="As_An_T_Check_FirstFlow" sourceRef="An_T_Check_FirstFlow" targetRef="T_Check_FirstFlow" />
    <textAnnotation id="An_T_Verdict">
      <text>The verdict sets the HTTP status of the answer through
WorkflowEnvironment.Variables[StatusCode], as the built-in
setResponseStatus does: 200 when every check passed, 500
when any failed. The body is the report either way.</text>
    </textAnnotation>
    <association id="As_An_T_Verdict" sourceRef="An_T_Verdict" targetRef="T_Verdict" />

  </process>
